# Output folder

Every file this plugin creates goes in `adrenaline/software-architect/` at the project root.

If `.cursor/adrenaline.json` exists and `outputDirs["plugin-software-architect"]` holds a path, use that path. The path is relative to the project root, with no `..` and not absolute. If it is not valid, use `adrenaline/software-architect/` and say so.

If `adrenaline/software-architect/` does not exist yet and `software-architect/` at the project root already has this plugin's `ORIGIN.json` or `STATUS.md`, keep writing there and say so.

Create the folder if it does not exist. Do not write anywhere else.

When the person names one project, app, service, or domain, put that subject's files in `<subject>/` (kebab-case, the name they used). A file about the whole product stays at this folder's root. `<NNN>` is the next free number in the whole output folder. `STATUS.md` and `ORIGIN.json` stay at the root. The `archivo` cell is `<subject>/<file>` when there is a subject. This is `adrenaline/software-architect/008-adr-asunto-subcarpeta.md`.

Write the artifact in the language of the request. If the request names a language, use that one. Otherwise use the language the request is written in. Keep names the person already used. The type in the file name stays the English piece id. `STATUS.md` columns stay `N`, `archivo`, `estado`, `sustituye`, `notas`.

Keep `ORIGIN.json` in that folder, beside `STATUS.md`. The fields are `suite` `ADRenaline-Suite`, `plugin` `plugin-software-architect`, `repository` `https://github.com/ADRenaline-Suite/plugin-software-architect`, and `convention` `adr-001`. It is not an `<NNN>` file and it has no row in `STATUS.md`. Write it when the folder is created, and again only if it is missing or a field differs.
